---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sandkasten | Ray Weiss"
  description="Sandkasten. Open-source naval and air wargame. Free in the browser at csl-sandkasten.com. Designed by Ray Weiss, Conflict Simulations LLC."
>
  <main class="doc">
    <div class="doc__frame">
      <header class="page-heading">
        <nav class="eyebrow" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/conflict-simulations-llc"
            >Conflict Simulations LLC</a
          >
        </nav>
        <h1>Sandkasten</h1>
        <p class="dek">Open-source naval and air wargame. Free in your browser.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-body">
        <p>
          Command naval and air forces on a tactical map with NATO symbology, radar detection, fog
          of war, and continuous or WeGo turns. Designed by Ray Weiss at Conflict Simulations LLC.
          The live build sits at <a href="https://csl-sandkasten.com">csl-sandkasten.com</a>, not on
          itch.
        </p>
        <p>
          The demo scenario puts a US carrier strike group in the Strait of Hormuz: bring USS Nimitz
          into the marked transit gate. Sensors and fog decide what you see; missiles and air
          defence fight it out. A scenario editor lets you place your own forces.
        </p>
        <p>
          Shares its map renderer and NATO symbology with Auftragstaktik. Platform data is
          community-maintained and open. Free and open source.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/games/sandkasten-cover.png"
          alt="Sandkasten play view: green tactical plot of the Strait of Hormuz with Nimitz group tracks, range rings and a mission sidebar"
          width="800"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Play view, Strait of Hormuz</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="prose-body terminal-section">
        <h2>Play</h2>
        <p>
          Free in the browser at
          <a href="https://csl-sandkasten.com">csl-sandkasten.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
